WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.530
- So on your podcast,

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.363
with Nicole,

00:00:02.363 --> 00:00:04.710
you said hot dogs are your love language.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.543
Is that true?

00:00:05.543 --> 00:00:06.530
Do you like hot dogs that much?

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:07.900
- I love hot dogs.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.733
Yeah.

00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:09.566
I'm a little embarrassed to talk about it,

00:00:09.566 --> 00:00:11.000
but I love them

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.230
'cause I feel like I've talked to people

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.580
who are like, "Oh, what's the
best meal you've ever had?"

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.620
And they're like, "This pasta in Italy,"

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.630
or "Seafood by the bay".

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.811
And I'm like, "I had a great
hot dog at Magic Kingdom."

00:00:22.811 --> 00:00:23.832
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:23.832 --> 00:00:25.900
- [Sasheer] Really.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:26.980
Actually, funny story.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.470
Nicole was dating a guy

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.080
who worked at a hot dog shop

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.430
near my house in New York.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.350
- Jackpot for you.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:33.183
- [Sasheer] Yeah.

00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:35.380
I mean, he left the job years later,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.260
and then they met,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.580
you know, happenstance,

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.750
and he was like, "Weird question.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.230
Does your best friend
Sasheer like hot dogs?"

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.970
And she was like, "Yeah, she loves them."

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:47.400
And he was like, "Yeah, she
would often come alone."

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.168
And I was like, "He
didn't have to say alone."

00:00:49.168 --> 00:00:50.850
(audience laughs)

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.329
- He didn't have to drive it like that.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:53.162
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:53.162 --> 00:00:54.480
- [Sasheer] Just say I went there a bunch,

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.050
like don't tell other people
I was there alone often.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.260
- [Kelly] And what's wrong with that?

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.093
- Exactly.

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:01.926
- There's nothing wrong with that.

00:01:01.926 --> 00:01:03.300
- Yeah.
- I wanted a hot dog.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.133
I went and got a hot dog.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.120
I go places by myself.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.220
That's what happens when you're single.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.370
- I'm an independent woman.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:08.507
- [Kelly] Yes.
- If I want a hot dog,

00:01:08.507 --> 00:01:09.340
I'm gonna get a hot dog.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.173
(audience cheers)

00:01:10.173 --> 00:01:11.006
- [Kelly] It also happens

00:01:11.006 --> 00:01:11.839
when you're a single woman with children

00:01:11.839 --> 00:01:14.080
and you're like, "Someone
watch them. I need a minute."

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:15.130
- [Sasheer] Exactly.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.420
- I don't wanna surround
myself with people.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.253
There are people at home.

00:01:17.253 --> 00:01:18.740
- [Sasheer] Yeah. This
is a private me time.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.620
Need my hot dog.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.150
- [Kelly] I love me time.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.270
- I had a husband whose idea of a great,

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.540
it was the middle one,

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.408
his idea of a great vacation
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:27.408 --> 00:01:30.210
was traveling around the country

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.750
to all the baseball stadiums.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.320
So I decided my role

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.580
was to figure out which
one had the best hot dogs.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.413
Kansas City.

00:01:38.413 --> 00:01:39.246
- Ooh?

00:01:39.246 --> 00:01:40.770
- Kansas City Royals, their stadium.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.603
Oh my God. Best.

00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:42.436
- Good to know.

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:43.269
I'll have to go there.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.212
- Yeah, really.

00:01:44.212 --> 00:01:45.130
- I love that that was
something that y'all did.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.160
Just go to stadiums.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:46.993
That's awesome.

